 "summary_html": "<p>In metal typesetting, a <b>font</b> is a particular size, weight, and style of a typeface, a set of fonts that share an overall design.\nFor instance, the typeface Bauer Bodoni includes fonts \"Roman 12pt\", \"<b>bold 12pt</b>\" and \"<i>italic 12pt</i><span>\"</span>; each of these styles is also available in a range of other common sizes. In traditional printing, fonts were physically created using metal or wood type, with a font for each size.</p>",
 "summary_text": "In metal typesetting, a font is a particular size, weight, and style of a typeface, a set of fonts that share an overall design.\nFor instance, the typeface Bauer Bodoni includes fonts \"Roman 12pt\", \"bold 12pt\" and \"italic 12pt\"; each of these styles is also available in a range of other common sizes. In traditional printing, fonts were physically created using metal or wood type, with a font for each size.",
